# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Growlith Engine — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit a filled-in copy: every dotenv
# file except this one is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# RULES
#  1. Placeholders only in this file. If a real value is ever committed here it
#     must be treated as compromised and rotated.
#  2. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are INLINED INTO THE BROWSER BUNDLE at build time.
#     They are public. Anything not prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` never reaches the
#     client.
#  3. `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` holds Supabase's `service_role`, which has the
#     PostgreSQL BYPASSRLS attribute. It defeats every Row Level Security policy
#     at once. It must never be prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_`, never logged, and never
#     imported outside `src/server/**`.
#  4. Variables are declared here only once something in this repository
#     consumes them. Auth and rate-limit configuration arrive with Phase 3 and
#     Phase 6 respectively; no speculative keys are listed (Rule 14).
#
#     Deliberately absent: the Supabase connection strings
#     (`SUPABASE_DB_URL_POOLED`, `SUPABASE_DB_URL_DIRECT`). Application code
#     never opens a PostgreSQL connection — all database access goes through
#     Supabase's API — so these are migration tooling, and Phase 2 adds them
#     together with the migration runner that reads them. See
#     `supabase/README.md` for which one migrations require and why.
#
# The authoritative contract lives in code, not here:
#   client-exposed → src/lib/env/client-env.ts   (CLIENT_ENV_KEYS)
#   server-only    → src/server/env.ts           (SERVER_ENV_KEYS)
# tests/architecture/env-contract.spec.ts fails if this file and those lists
# disagree, so the template cannot silently rot.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# development | staging | production
# At `production` an incomplete environment crashes the process at boot rather
# than failing later inside a request. Elsewhere it logs a warning.
APP_ENV=development

# debug | info | warn | error | silent
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Canonical origin of this deployment, e.g. https://portal.growlithacademy.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Supabase: public ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project URL. Safe to expose.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co

# Anonymous key. Safe to expose ONLY because Row Level Security exists: it grants
# exactly what RLS permits for the authenticated user, and nothing more.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_ANON_KEY

# ── Supabase: server-only (NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_) ───────────────────
# service_role key. BYPASSRLS. Confined to src/server/supabase/client-service.ts.
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role secret.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
